{John already stood worse when he blundered a piece with 28 Ng5. Then Nigel
made the classic blunder of blitzing his opponent, while in time-trouble. So
much so that he made about 4 moves consecutively, without writing down the
score - which incidentally, is against the rules. 32...Nxf4 seems to have been
Black's best chance of winning. After that opportunity passed, he could do
nothing right and Blak seemed to lose any sense of danger. 40...Nf5 may have
held.} 1. c4 g6 2. Nc3 Bg7 3. g3 c5 4. Bg2 Nc6 5. e3 Nh6 6. Nge2 Nf5 7. b3 b6
8. Bb2 Bb7 9. Qb1 O-O 10. O-O e6 11. Nf4 Na5 12. Bxb7 Nxb7 13. Nce2 Na5 14.
