{Again Black made much of the running. An exciting game, but perhaps Mark
should have gone really swash-buckling with 14 h4. 27 Be3 would have been much
better than Re5 and White eventually changed those moves around at some cost
in time. Willie felt that life was unfair, in that he won a pawn, played quite
accurately, but never seemed to be winning. 38 b3 would have been a spirited
winning try.} 1. e4 c5 2. f4 g6 3. Nf3 Bg7 4. Nc3 Nc6 5. Bb5 Nd4 6. a4 e6 7. e5
