{Paul Motwani has done little in chess since winning the World u-17
Championship, because he has been concentrating on his studies. His claim to
have once played in England, in Newcastle, was quickly rejected. Here he had
slightly the worse of it and was in terrible time-trouble, but Shaun was
unable to clinch a win. Perhaps 35...a4 was the moment of truth.} 1. d4 Nf6 2.
