{John Cox seems to have an extremely cavalier attitude towards pieces. So far
in this tournament, his results have justified this atitude. Surely the piece
must have been better than the 3 pawns initially? Still, yet another
uncompromising struggle and also a great rarity in master chess, a round with
all games having positive results.} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5.
