{Mark likes clear-cut attacking positions, and is relatively ill at ease when
he has little to do. Shaun achieved this type of game and duly reaped the
rewards 26...Ba8 sacrificing the exchange after 27 c5 looks better. When
material down, it is not uaually best to swap pieces but 39...Qxe1 lands White
in an endgame that looks very drawish. It seems imposssible to push the b-pawn
past b6 without using the bishop - and that would weaken the kingside
excessively.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 g6 3. Bf4 Bg7 4. e3 d6 5. h3 O-O 6. Be2 c5 7. c3
