{Perhaps 10...Bg4 followed by Nd7 is a little more accurate. The first pawn
sacrifice with 12...c4 may be sound, but then Black's queenside became too
weak so that more pawns had to be shed. There was never enough play on the
queenside to justify this.} 1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 c5 3. d5 e6 4. Nc3 exd5 5. cxd5 d6
6. e4 g6 7. Nf3 Bg7 8. Be2 O-O 9. O-O Re8 10. Qc2 Na6 11. Re1 Bg4 12. Bf4 c4
