{Probably the best game of the tournament to date. I would be extremely
reluctant to comment on the tactics in the middlegame, except to say that
Blacl always seemed to have compensation for hgis various pawns sacrificed.
Although White had the outside passed pawn in the endame reached, Black stood
better because the e3 pawn was weak. The sealed move 44.Nc8 seems strange, but
White feared the position resulting after 44 Nc4 Qe6 45 Qxe6 fxe6. A game too
long to find its way into newspaper columns, but nonetheless one that makes
these events worthwhile..} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 Nf6 5. O-O Be7
