{Paul seemed annoyed at the aspersions cast on the weakness of his tripled
pawns. After all, he did have an extra baby! 26 Qa1 looks a bizarre
decentralisation. Perhaps 27...f5 weakens the e-pawn too much, but jettisoning
a pawn with 31...Qf6 was unnecessary. Even then it was difficult for White to
win, because his extra pawns were so fragile. Stuart commented that his play
seems to go off in the 5th hour, Harry Golombek questions his endgame
technique. Of course, both technical deficiences are remediable.} 1. e4 c5 2.
