{Shaun was most scathing about his own game, claiming errors on nearly every
move. 7 e5 was perhaps a little previous. 8 e6 is questionable pawn sacrifice.
10 h4 seems to be a slow way of proceeding. 12 Bxc5 followed by Bc4 would have
given White a satisfactory game. 13 Nxb5 is a better way to capture. 14 Bxc5
followed by Bc4 is still best. Shaun is perhaps beng over-particular and let
us no take Nigel's triumph away from him. 18 b4 was just one way of going down.
} 1. d4 g6 2. e4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Be3 Nf6 5. h3 O-O 6. Nf3 Na6 7. e5 Nd7 8. e6
