{Apparently after the players agreed a draw after an hour's play, they then
went off and analysed the final position for 2 hours. Harry Golombek tells me
that he once saw two players agree an instant draw and they then went to a
side-room, where they continued playing the game "for real". These 3 draws may
have been in protest at the early start to the last round - beloved of many
organisers, but an anathema to most players. I had opposed this when we set up
the tournament. The games almost never continue endlessly and the event is
arranged for the players, not the controllers. However, he players do have a
responsibility to the sponsors and these instant draws are extremely negative
for public relations.} 1. e4 c5 2. f4 e6 3. Nf3 a6 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nxd4 d6 6. Nc3
Nf6 7. Bd3 Nbd7 8. O-O b5 9. a3 Bb7 10. Kh1 Be7 11. b4 O-O 12. Qe1 1/2-1/2

