{When Shaun is at his best he seems better able than most to obtain positions
in which his opponents are ill at ease. He took the initiative away from
Hebden and here keeps the position simple. Black had to safeguard his centre
against the thrust f5 before embarking on any queenside sortie. After it came,
he was practically helpless.} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 Nc6 4. Ngf3 Nf6 5. e5
